    /// approval_key_unavailable without a live approval key. Answers a challenge (single use, 120 s, bound to this
    /// session, the family and the target) and payload_b64, the exact bytes to sign: "vh-device-approval-v1" 0x00
    /// node_id 0x00 server_spki_sha256[32] approving_device_spki_sha256[32] challenge[32] family 0x00 target 0x00
    /// UInt64BE(expires_at). The device checks them against what it knows before asking for Touch ID. At most 4 open
    /// per session (a new one replaces the oldest).
    case deviceApprovalChallenge = "device.approval.challenge"
    /// Register this already-paired device's approval key (once per device): a P-256 SubjectPublicKeyInfo, 91 bytes of
    /// DER, standard base64, not the connection's key. A person approves it in the web console: it answers
    /// step_up_required (device.trust, target device.approval.key.register:<device row>:<key SPKI SHA-256>) until a
    /// console approval (device.approval.request) for exactly that target. conflict: the device has (or had) a key, or
    /// the key is known here.
    case deviceApprovalKeyRegister = "device.approval.key.register"
    /// Ask a person to approve a step-up in the web console (any family; the one way for families the approval key
    /// can't approve, and for a device without one). summary (1-160 characters) is shown with the family and target.
    /// The account's console sessions get auth.approval.pending; a person approves with a passkey
    /// (auth.approval.approve). Lives 5 minutes; at most 3 open and 10 per hour per device (rate_limited). Poll
    /// device.approval.status on this same session.
    case deviceApprovalRequest = "device.approval.request"
    /// How a console approval stands (pending, approved, denied, expired). Answered at once: ask again in 2 s while
    /// pending. Once approved, the first answer leaves the grant on this session (the same binding as a web session's:
    /// target-bound grants are spent by one use); then resend the refused request. Only the session that asked: another
    /// is not_found.
    case deviceApprovalStatus = "device.approval.status"
    /// Answer a challenge with the approval key's ECDSA P-256/SHA-256 signature (DER, standard base64) over its
    /// payload. The challenge is spent whatever the answer. On success this session holds a grant for the family and
    /// target (spent by one use, until expires_at); then resend the refused request. invalid: the signature doesn't
    /// verify (the payload as the server computes it now: a changed node or server key never verifies); not_found:
    /// expired, used or another session's; approval_key_unavailable: the key was revoked.
    case deviceApprovalSubmit = "device.approval.submit"
    /// Confirm a live grant: a migrated one becomes approved, a suspended one exports again. device.trust approval for
    /// target device.backup.grant.confirm:<grant>.
    case deviceBackupGrantConfirm = "device.backup.grant.confirm"
    /// Turn on key backup for vaults on one of the caller's devices: on its own session the device itself, on a console
    /// session device_id. Needs the export encryption keys permission (or super admin) and a device.trust approval for
    /// target device.backup.grant.create:<device row>:<vault ids> (step_up_required names it). conflict: the device
    /// already has a grant (extend it). During a recovery cooldown only the device re-creates the grant the recovery
    /// revoked, with its approval key registered before the recovery, for vaults that grant named (recovery_cooldown
