    case deviceBackupGrantCreate = "device.backup.grant.create"
    /// Add vaults to a live grant of the caller's (a new vault, one deliberate approval). device.trust approval for
    /// target device.backup.grant.extend:<grant>:<vault ids>. conflict: it names them all already, or it was revoked.
    case deviceBackupGrantExtend = "device.backup.grant.extend"
    /// Key-backup grants: on a console session the caller's (every device, live first, revoked ones after); on a paired
    /// device's session that device's only. A grant lets its device export the keys of the vaults it names with no
    /// prompt (Desktop's background 1Password backup). A grant whose revocation trigger holds (device revoked or idle
    /// 90 days, account deactivated or without the Export permission) is revoked before it is listed.
    case deviceBackupGrantList = "device.backup.grant.list"
    /// Turn key backup off for a device: revokes the grant (its owner, the device itself, or a super admin). Needs no
    /// approval. Final: a new grant is a new create.
    case deviceBackupGrantRevoke = "device.backup.grant.revoke"
    /// Where this node's device listener can be reached (docs/reference/transfer-protocol.md §1.1): interface addresses
    /// classified by range, <hostname>.local where an mDNS responder runs, and device_server.advertise's configured
    /// names. Computed per call; never answered before a device is paired.
    case deviceEndpoints = "device.endpoints"
    /// Replace this device's key: certificate is the new self-signed P-256 certificate (base64 DER), signature the old
    /// key's ECDSA-P256-SHA256 (base64 DER) over "vh-device-rotate-v1" ‖ new_spki_sha256 ‖ server_spki_sha256 ‖
    /// UInt64BE(timestamp). The old key keeps working until the first connection with the new one. A retry from the old
    /// key naming the same new key succeeds again; another key is conflict.
    case deviceIdentityRotate = "device.identity.rotate"
    /// The caller's devices, revoked ones included; with all, every user's (super admins only).
    case deviceList = "device.list"
    /// Reveal nonce_device. It must match the request's commitment (else the request is deleted: invalid); then the
