    /// hosts can reach it (remote), and what the vaulthalla://pair link carries (node_id, server_spki_sha256,
    /// endpoints; transfer-protocol.md §1.2).
    case devicePairingOpen = "device.pairing.open"
    /// The caller's open window and its confirmed requests. Each offers three code_choices (random order): one is the
    /// code the device shows, two are decoys fixed for the request. The real code is never returned on its own. Also
    /// answered on a paired device's session (an already-paired Desktop approving a new one, design 8.4);
    /// approval_key_present says the request carries an approval key.
    case devicePairingPending = "device.pairing.pending"
    /// Back to loopback only: the listener rebinds now and device sessions from other hosts close.
    case deviceRemoteDisable = "device.remote.disable"
    /// Let devices on other hosts connect: the listener rebinds to every interface now, and stays that way across
    /// restarts and upgrades (device_server.remote in config.yaml).
    case deviceRemoteEnable = "device.remote.enable"
    /// The device listener: loopback only or every interface, and whether it listens; diagnostics say where it is
    /// bound, what devices are told, what the host firewall looks like (read-only, null when unknown) and when a device
    /// last connected from a public address.
    case deviceRemoteStatus = "device.remote.status"
    /// Rename a device (its user, or a super admin).
    case deviceRename = "device.rename"
    /// Unpair a device (its user, a super admin, or the device itself). Final: its live sessions close at once and its
    /// key only ever gets pairing-only connections again. A scoped device may unpair only itself (device_scope).
    case deviceRevoke = "device.revoke"
    /// Change a device's scope (read, write or destructive). Narrowing: the device's user or a super admin, no step-up.
