    /// subscription ends with the session.
    case healthSubscribe = "health.subscribe"
    /// Stop following the health findings by push (health.subscribe). Harmless when not subscribed.
    case healthUnsubscribe = "health.unsubscribe"
    /// The contract this daemon was built from: contract_version, contract_hash (the whole document vh_usage --json
    /// publishes), ws_hash (the ws command book, what the web console is generated from) and models_hash (the model
    /// shapes the book refers to). Read-only, no secrets; needs a signed-in session (no build fingerprinting before
    /// login).
    case metaContractGet = "meta.contract.get"
    /// The protocol handshake, first thing after connecting (after sign-in on the web socket; allowed where
    /// meta.contract.get is: signed-in web, paired device and pairing-only sessions, never an unauthenticated or share
    /// session). The client says what it is and the protocol range it speaks; the daemon answers its own name and
    /// version, the protocol version this session now speaks (the newest both speak; kProtocolMin without a range, as
    /// for a session that never says hello), its own range, its capabilities, every command it registers and its
    /// contract identity. No overlap: ERROR protocol_unsupported with data {code, server_min, server_max,
    /// server_version}. A paired device's client.version refreshes its app_version.
    case metaHello = "meta.hello"
    /// Accept an offer (super admins): checked again (mirror_vault_exists, mirror_name_taken, mirror_no_space,
    /// history_not_supported), then the core is told and sends the keys.
    case mirrorAccept = "mirror.accept"
    /// Whether this server accepts every vault a linked server offers without asking (default off). Super admins;
    /// audited mirror.accept_all.set.
    case mirrorAcceptAllSet = "mirror.accept_all.set"
    /// Start mirroring one of this server's vaults to a linked server (this server stays its core). Every precondition
