        case .vaultKeysRecipientsRevoke:
            """
            Revoke a recovery recipient: no new envelopes are written for it (a recipient the account's signed\
             recovery policy added is refused recovery_policy_account_managed). Access it already has is not revoked\
             (an envelope keeps unwrapping the versions it covers): recovery.rotation_needed says when a key rotation\
             is needed to cut it off from new data. Paired devices only (recipient_requires_device otherwise), with a\
             keys step-up bound to the vault (#359); the encryption-key Export permission.
            """
        case .vaultKeysStatus:
            """
            Key backup state of every vault the caller may inspect (the encryption-key View permission; deleted vaults\
             within key retention for callers who may remove them), or of vault_id. Never key bytes: each key version\
             is identified by its key_check. Read-only; safe for any session.
            """
        case .vaultLayoutCleanup:
            """
            After the cutover and its waiting period: the legacy (path-named) objects a cleanup would delete by\
             version id, and those that stay (a dry run without confirm). With confirm set to the vault's name the\
             cleanup is confirmed and runs in the background (a data.destroy step-up bound to the vault, #359). Never\
             on a protected bucket, never a version under Object Lock retention or a legal hold. The encryption-key\
             Rotate permission.
            """
        case .vaultLayoutMigrate:
            """
            Start (or resume after a failure) the vault's bucket layout migration path_v0 -> opaque_v1: it runs in the\
             background (vault.layout.status follows it). Refused (conflict) when the vault can't migrate now (not an\
             encrypting S3 vault on path_v0, a rotation or salvage, a key version not held, no recovery material, a\
             protected bucket) or already migrates. With a keys step-up bound to the vault (#359); the encryption-key\
             Rotate permission.
            """
        case .vaultLayoutStatus:
            """
            The vault's bucket layout and its migration path_v0 -> opaque_v1 (#373): state, the cost estimate and\
             usage, inventory counts, and every legacy version that stays in the bucket with its reason. The\
             encryption-key View permission.
            """
        case .vaultRecover:
            """
            Rebuild a vault on this instance from its bucket and the customer's recovery material (#371, spec 03 §6):\
             a recovery kit (its seed unwraps the vault's KEV1 envelopes) and/or a key export. A key version is\
             restored only when its original node's attestation verifies against an attestation key the material pins\
             (D1); otherwise the answer is salvage_required with the per-version verdicts, and salvage (confirmed with\
             confirm_name) re-encrypts what the supplied keys decrypt under a fresh key, never storing them. dry_run\
             reads and reports, writing nothing. The vault starts in the cache strategy: nothing beyond headers, the\
             manifest and envelopes is downloaded until a file is read. Paired devices only (recover_requires_device\
             otherwise), with a keys step-up bound to the bucket; the encryption-key Export permission and vault\
             Create.
            """
        case .vaultRecoveryDisclosure:
            """
            The cost disclosure a person must see before provider versioning is enabled, with the token\
             vault.recovery.update needs (10 minutes). Read-only: at most one admin inspect, no object requests.
            """
        case .vaultRecoveryStatus:
            """
            A vault's recovery mode, local versioning, store usage, upstream backlog and provider versioning state;\
             refresh_provider re-reads the bucket (one admin round trip).
            """
        case .vaultRecoverySuspend:
            """
            Suspend versioning on the vault's bucket (AWS S3); existing versions are kept and nothing is deleted. A\
             refusal with data.code 'recovery_versioning_suspend' asks for confirmation: resend with confirm.\
             Backblaze B2 can't suspend (invalid): set mode off to keep only the latest version.
            """
        case .vaultRecoveryUpdate:
            """
            Change a vault's recovery settings. mode provider_versioning needs disclosure_token from\
             vault.recovery.disclosure ('recovery_versioning_disclosure'); unpriced costs need accept_unpriced\
             ('recovery_versioning_unpriced'); a shorter retention needs accept_retention_shortening\
             ('recovery_retention_shorten') and a data.destroy step-up; the vault's unmanaged bucket needs\
             accept_adoption ('upstream_adoption'). On Backblaze B2, mode off or local_snapshots also makes the bucket\
             keep only the latest version, asked with 'recovery_retention_shorten' (and the step-up) when that deletes\
             history that exists now.
            """
        case .vaultRemoteAbort:
            """
            Abort an attach or a detach before its cutover. An attach's abort deletes everything it uploaded from the\
             bucket, each object by the version the attach recorded, in the background, and releases the bucket (state\
             aborted); nothing the attach did not write is deleted, the vault itself was never changed, and a delete\
             the provider refuses is retried and stays listed. A detach's abort leaves the vault an S3 vault; the\
             local copies it fetched stay. confirm must be the vault's name. With a keys step-up bound to the vault\
             (#359); the same permissions as vault.remote.attach, without the API key's.
            """
        case .vaultRemoteAttach:
            """
            Attach a bucket to a local vault (design/storage/attach-remote.md): the vault keeps its id, keys,\
             permissions, shares and files and becomes an encrypting S3/R2 vault in place. Checks every precondition\
             now (a local vault with its keys loaded, no key rotation or salvage, no content in a legacy format, every\
             key version held and attested, recovery material independent of this host, an empty bucket no vault\
             holds, a bucket that can publish the manifest) and probes the bucket; then the upload runs in the\
             background and resumes after a restart (vault.remote.status follows it). Nothing of the vault changes\
             before the cutover. A failed attach started again with the same API key and bucket resumes. With a keys\
             step-up bound to the vault (#359). Needs the vault's admin Edit and sync config Edit permissions, the API\
             key's Consume permission and the encryption-key Rotate permission.
            """
        case .vaultRemoteDetach:
            """
            Detach the remote of an S3 vault (design/storage/attach-remote.md, "The reverse"): the vault keeps its id,\
             keys, permissions, shares and files and becomes a local vault in place. Checks the preconditions now (an\
             S3 vault with its keys loaded, no attach, layout migration, key rotation or salvage running, no content\
             in a legacy format, every key version its files use held, no event-driven sync, no open sync conflict);\
             then in the background every file without a local copy is fetched, every local copy is authenticated, and\
             every recovery envelope is copied from the bucket into the database, before the vault switches in one\
             transaction. The bucket and its objects are left in place. vault.remote.status follows it; a failed\
             detach started again resumes. confirm must be the vault's name. With a keys step-up bound to the vault\
             (#359); the vault's admin Edit and sync config Edit permissions and the encryption-key Rotate permission.
            """
        case .vaultRemoteStatus:
            """
            Where attaching (or detaching) a remote stands for vault_id, or for every vault with an attach or detach\
             the caller may view: state, bucket, publish mode, progress (files and bytes, rate, time left), the\
             estimate and usage, the last error, and after an attach's cutover the first sync pass's result. The\
             vault's admin View permission. Read-only; safe for any session.
            """
        case .vaultStorageProbe:
            """
            Probe what the vault's bucket supports for writes that must never overwrite another writer's object\
             (design/encryption/06-publish-without-preconditions.md §7): conditional PUT honoured, rejected or\
             ignored, object versions, GET If-Match. About ten requests under .vaulthalla/probe/, whose versions are\
             deleted by id afterwards. Records the verdict, which replaces a bucket_capability_changed mark. The\
             vault's admin Edit permission; refused (denied) on a protected bucket, bucket_probe_failed when the\
             bucket can't be reached.
            """
        }
    }
}
